# Omarchy migrations that Software Update may run with root without a person (ADR-0033 s5, owner decision SU-M2; rc7 audit
# R7-SEC-01). Installed as /usr/share/grassfield/update/omarchy-migrations.allow (root's alone): grassfield-update-helper
# uses its migrations' unit only when every migration the run would run there is an `allow` line here, by sha256 and name,
# and checks the installed file again just before it runs; anything else takes Omarchy's terminal. This list is the
# guarantee; the helper's word scans are defence in depth.
# GENERATED by scripts/dev/omarchy-migrations-allow.py from each supported Omarchy release (one per docs/upstream/omarchy*.lock,
# the same trees as the drift review): `allow` = the helper's scans find neither a person's step nor code of the home folder.
# Review the `allow` lines of a new release with its drift review before committing them; tests/shell/omarchy_migrations_allow.sh
# fails while a supported release is not listed whole.
#   release <omarchy package> newest-migration <N> migrations <count>
#   allow   <sha256> <name> <omarchy package>
#   exclude <sha256> <name> <omarchy package> <person|home-code|review|unreadable>
# (review: the generator's wider patterns, stricter than the helper's runtime scan: other interpreters and package builders,
# login, interactive or -c shells, eval, exec, input read from or code under a home path, the XDG folders, /home/)
